   "DisplayFormula", CellFrameLabels -> {{None, "(38)"}, {None, None}}], 
  Cell["Subtract the steady-state log identities to remove constant shares. \
Conditional on fixed total C and other relative prices, a one-log-percent \
rise in pF raises pc by \[Omega]F, reduces food demand by 1\[Minus]\[Omega]F, \
and raises domestic demand by \[Omega]F. Full equilibrium consumption and \
policy are not held fixed in an impulse response.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[StyleBox["C", 
         FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False], TraditionalForm], 
       FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], "=", 
      RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[RowBox[{"(", FractionBox[
            RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[SubscriptBox[StyleBox["C", 
                  FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False], StyleBox["N", 
                  FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False]], 
                TraditionalForm], FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]]}], 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{"1", RowBox[{"-", RowBox[
                     {FormBox[SubscriptBox["\[Omega]", StyleBox["E", 
                         FontSlant -> Plain, StripOnInput -> False]], 
                       TraditionalForm]}]}]}], ")"}]}]], ")"}], 
         RowBox[{"1", RowBox[{"-", RowBox[{FormBox[SubscriptBox["\[Omega]", 
                 StyleBox["E", FontSlant -> Plain, StripOnInput -> False]], 
                TraditionalForm]}]}]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        SuperscriptBox[RowBox[{"(", FractionBox[RowBox[
             {SubscriptBox[FormBox[SubscriptBox[StyleBox["C", FontSlant -> 
                   Italic, StripOnInput -> False], StyleBox["E", FontSlant -> 
                   Plain, StripOnInput -> False]], TraditionalForm], FormBox[
                "t", TraditionalForm]]}], RowBox[{FormBox[SubscriptBox[
                "\[Omega]", StyleBox["E", FontSlant -> Plain, StripOnInput -> 
                  False]], TraditionalForm]}]], ")"}], 
         FormBox[SubscriptBox["\[Omega]", StyleBox["E", FontSlant -> Plain, 
            StripOnInput -> False]], TraditionalForm]]}]}]], 
   "DisplayFormula", CellFrameLabels -> {{None, "(39)"}, {None, None}}], 
  Cell["Removing food gives this two-good basket and pc=\[Omega]E pE, with \
the same cn and ce log equations. At \[Omega]F=0 take the continuous \
reduced-model limit; do not insert zero directly into CF/\[Omega]F. \
Zero-share quantities cannot be log-linearised around a zero level.", 
   "Text"], Cell["4. Deflators, wages, monetary policy and domestic prices", 
   "Section"], Cell["A deflator converts a nominal amount into purchasing \
power measured in a particular good or basket. Suppose nominal earnings stay \
unchanged while household energy becomes more expensive. The wage measured in \
domestic goods can stay constant if the domestic-good price has not changed, \
yet the same earnings purchase less of the consumption basket. Hence w and wc \
answer different questions. The distinction is central when imported prices \
move independently of domestic prices.", "Text"], 
  Cell["The assumption of a domestic numeraire is a choice of units: dividing \
by PD does not assume that the domestic price is constant in nominal terms. \
Relative prices PE/PD and PC/PD can change, and domestic inflation pi remains \
an endogenous variable. A constant normalised steady relative price also does \
not prevent dynamic relative-price shocks.", "Text"], 
  Cell["4.1 Inflation accounting", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["The identity PC=PD\[CenterDot](PC/PD) implies that consumption \
inflation is domestic inflation plus the change in the relative consumption \
price. The same argument applies to each imported good. The term added to \
inflation is a price CHANGE, not the relative price level itself.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[TemplateBox[
         {"\[Pi]", StyleBox["C", FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> 
            False]}, "Superscript", SyntaxForm -> SuperscriptBox], 
        TraditionalForm], FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], "=", 
      RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox["\[Pi]", TraditionalForm], 
         FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], 
        RowBox[{"+", SubscriptBox[FormBox[SubscriptBox["p", 
             StyleBox["C", FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False]], 
            TraditionalForm], FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]]}], 
        RowBox[{"-", RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[SubscriptBox["p", StyleBox[
                "C", FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False]], 
              TraditionalForm], RowBox[{FormBox["t", TraditionalForm], RowBox[
                {"-", "1"}]}]]}]}]}]}]], "DisplayFormula", 
   CellFrameLabels -> {{None, "(40)"}, {None, None}}], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[TemplateBox[
         {"\[Pi]", StyleBox["E", FontSlant -> Plain, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
