              ")"}]}]}]}]}]], "DisplayFormula", 
   CellFrameLabels -> {{None, "(45)"}, {None, None}}], 
  Cell["The household's reservation-wage term depends on smoothed \
habit-adjusted consumption z, labour-supply wedge epsilons and employment e. \
comega=\[Omega]U and cv=vz. Classic uses w, since its PC=PD; sectoral \
versions use wc. A commodity-price increase can therefore lower consumption \
purchasing power at an unchanged domestic-real wage. Hours n and employment e \
remain distinct quantities.", "Text"], Cell["Wage rigidity means that \
households or wage setters cannot freely reset every wage in every period. A \
Calvo-style parameter thetaW can be interpreted as the probability that a \
wage is not reoptimised in a period under a constant-hazard formulation. The \
indexation coefficient gammaW describes how a wage that is not freshly \
optimised is mechanically updated with past inflation. Indexation and \
reoptimisation are therefore distinct: an indexed wage may change without the \
setter choosing a new optimal wage.", "Text"], Cell["The unemployment term \
summarises a gap between wage compensation and the reservation-wage side of \
the labour market. Higher unemployment and a wage-markup disturbance affect \
bargaining or wage-setting pressure through the implemented reduced block. A \
natural unemployment variable here is a model counterfactual, not an \
assertion that all observed unemployment is voluntary or that the benchmark \
is a welfare optimum.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
     {RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[SubscriptBox["w", StyleBox["C", 
            FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False]], TraditionalForm], 
         FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], 
        RowBox[{"-", RowBox[{SubscriptBox[FormBox[SubscriptBox["w", StyleBox[
                "C", FontSlant -> Italic, StripOnInput -> False]], 
              TraditionalForm], RowBox[{FormBox["t", TraditionalForm], RowBox[
                {"-", "1"}]}]]}]}], RowBox[{"+", SubscriptBox[
           FormBox[TemplateBox[{"\[Pi]", StyleBox["C", FontSlant -> Italic, 
               StripOnInput -> False]}, "Superscript", SyntaxForm -> 
              SuperscriptBox], TraditionalForm], FormBox["t", 
            TraditionalForm]]}]}], "=", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{FormBox[SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "W"], 
           TraditionalForm], "\[ThinSpace]", SubscriptBox[
           FormBox[TemplateBox[{"\[Pi]", StyleBox["C", FontSlant -> Italic, 
               StripOnInput -> False]}, "Superscript", SyntaxForm -> 
              SuperscriptBox], TraditionalForm], 
           RowBox[{FormBox["t", TraditionalForm], RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}]]}], 
        RowBox[{"+", RowBox[{FormBox["\[Beta]", TraditionalForm], 
            "\[ThinSpace]", RowBox[{SubscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalE]", 
               FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], "[", RowBox[{SubscriptBox[
