nad\\Artyku\[LSlash] - DSGE - Do \
poprawy\\SWW_energia_w_produkcji\\sww_energia_w_produkcji.mod | core \
equations: 60 | SHA256: \
50b66a22b36b6fb6d33c6e9ee420dff12eaba587a8e911b4c34357d1162ddc32", "Text"], 
  Cell["Additional local sources: all three \
Estimation_Setup/EA20_calibration.mod, EA20_measurement.mod and \
EA20_shocks.mod modules; calibration/derived_parameters.py; the food folder's \
README.md; and the energy-only steady-state function. This is a derivation of \
the local specifications, not an assertion that every extension or parameter \
value belongs to the original published SWW model.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Symbolic and source checks", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["The checks cover expenditure duality, optimal input demand, Euler's \
production identity, marginal cost, resource-share adding up, classic \
capital-output equivalence, habit algebra, wage deflators, zero-food CPI \
reduction, and the exact food-versus-energy equation differences. They do not \
establish empirical fit or a stable stochastic equilibrium.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Numbered core equation counts : True\nFood changes only CPI and \
sticky/flexible export financing among shared equations : True\nFour added \
food equations : True\nProduction shares add to one : True\nEuler identity : \
True\nCost-minimising inputs reproduce output : True\nMinimal variable cost : \
True\nTwo-good expenditure duality : True\nThree-good expenditure duality : \
True\nRelative CPI identity : True\nWeighted factor FOCs imply marginal cost \
: True\nResource shares add up : True\nEquivalent classic capital-output \
formulas : True\nHabit coefficient algebra : True\nWage-deflator identity : \
True\nZero-food log-price limit : True", "Program", FontSize -> 9, 
   CellHorizontalScrolling -> False]}, StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb", 
 WindowTitle -> "SWW: energy and food derivation", WindowSize -> {1150, 900}, 
